# Skill Routing Rules

Prithvi's full skill inventory and when to use each. **Rule zero: prefer the most
specific `ce-*` workflow skill over a generic role agent.** Role agents
(@backend-architect etc.) are a fallback for open-ended design work, not the default.

## Routing by lifecycle stage

### Explore / decide (before any code)
| Task | Skill |
|---|---|
| Vague idea → right-sized requirements plan | `ce-brainstorm` |
| Generate + evaluate options before choosing | `ce-ideate` |
| Second opinion / verdict on an approach or doc | `ce-pov` |
| Create/update product STRATEGY.md | `ce-strategy` |
| Review an existing plan/spec with role lenses | `ce-doc-review` |
| Market/trend/competitor research | `product-trend-researcher` |
| Sprint scoping, RICE/MoSCoW prioritization | `product-sprint-prioritizer` |

### Plan / build
| Task | Skill |
|---|---|
| Break work into a structured multi-step plan | `ce-plan` |
| Execute a plan/spec/clear build request end-to-end | `ce-work` |
| Fully autonomous: plan→implement→PR, hands-off | `lfg` (only when explicitly wanted) |
| Isolated branch/worktree before risky work | `ce-worktree` |
| Open-ended system/API/schema/infra design | `@backend-architect` |
| UI implementation, React, performance, a11y | `@engineering-frontend-developer` |
| CI/CD, Docker, IaC, deploy strategies | `@engineering-devops-automator` |
| Laravel/Livewire/FluxUI/Three.js premium builds | `@engineering-senior-developer` |
| Anything touching Supabase | `supabase` |
| Postgres query/schema/perf work | `supabase-postgres-best-practices` |

### Debug / improve
| Task | Skill |
|---|---|
| Bugs, stack traces, failing tests, stuck fixes | `ce-debug` (NOT a role agent) |
| Tidy/refactor recently changed code | `ce-simplify-code` |
| Metric-driven optimization loops | `ce-optimize` |
| In-browser polish pass on a feature | `ce-polish` |
| Browser tests for current branch/PR | `ce-test-browser` |
| iOS simulator build+test | `ce-test-xcode` |
| Hands-off browser QA of active branch | `ce-dogfood` (manual invocation only) |

### Ship / review
| Task | Skill |
|---|---|
| Pre-PR structured code review | `ce-code-review` |
| Commit with a good message | `ce-commit` |
| Commit + push + open PR | `ce-commit-push-pr` |
| Watch a PR to merge-ready (CI, comments, rebases) | `ce-babysit-pr` |
| Address/resolve PR review feedback | `ce-resolve-pr-feedback` |

### After shipping / knowledge
| Task | Skill |
|---|---|
| Capture a solved problem or project vocabulary | `ce-compound` |
| Audit stale/drifted docs/solutions learnings | `ce-compound-refresh` |
| Durable teaching artifact / deep explainer | `ce-explain` |
| Session handoff to another agent/session | `ce-handoff` |
| Publish/share specs or drafts in Proof | `ce-proof` |
| Launch/promo copy for a shipped feature | `ce-promote` |
| Time-windowed product pulse report | `ce-product-pulse` |
| Sweep Slack/GitHub feedback sources | `ce-sweep` |
| Analyze Riffrec recordings/bundles | `ce-riffrec-feedback-analysis` |
| Check compound-engineering repo config | `ce-setup` |

## Anti-patterns
- Don't use `@backend-architect` for a bug — that's `ce-debug`.
- Don't use `ce-work` for open-ended bugs — `ce-work` executes plans, `ce-debug` diagnoses.
- Don't hand-write commits/PRs — `ce-commit` / `ce-commit-push-pr`.
- Don't use `lfg` unless fully autonomous shipping was explicitly requested.
- Don't stack a role agent on top of a `ce-*` skill that already covers the job.
- After solving anything non-obvious, end with `ce-compound` to capture the learning.

## Conventions
- Always check and follow rules in `.cursor/rules/`.
- Never paste explicit SQL into prompts — let the agent discover schema.
